  "_9-JP0TEsEe6GxLzpkVnWYg": "Unique identification, as assigned by the first instructing agent, to unambiguously identify the transaction that is passed on, unchanged, throughout the entire interbank chain. |Usage: The transaction identification can be used for reconciliation, tracking or to link tasks relating to the transaction on the interbank level. |Usage: The instructing agent has to make sure that the transaction identification is unique for a pre-agreed period.",
