  "_Qdr_k9p-Ed-ak6NoX_4Aeg_1064399328": "Reuters Identification Code (RIC). A numbering system used within the Reuters system to identify instruments worldwide. The RIC contains an X-character market specific code (can be the CUSIP or EPIC codes) followed by a full stop, then the two-digit ISO country code, eg, IBM in UK is IBM.UK.",
  "_Qdr_kNp-Ed-ak6NoX_4Aeg_1064399268": "International Securities Identification Number (ISIN). A numbering system designed by the United Nation's International Organisation for Standardisation (ISO). The ISIN is composed of a 2-character prefix representing the country of issue, followed by the national security number (if one exists), and a check digit. Each country has a national numbering agency that assigns ISIN numbers for securities in that country.",
  "_Qdr_kdp-Ed-ak6NoX_4Aeg_1796754500": "Stock Exchange Daily Official List (SEDOL) number. A code used by the London Stock Exchange to identify foreign stocks, especially those that aren't actively traded in the US and don't have a CUSIP number.",
  "_Qdr_ktp-Ed-ak6NoX_4Aeg_-1393682718": "Committee on Uniform Securities and Identification Procedures (CUSIP). The standards body that created and maintains the securities classification system in the US. The CUSIP is composed of a 9-character number that uniquely identifies a particular security. Non-US securities have a similar number called the CINS number.",
  "_Qdr_l9p-Ed-ak6NoX_4Aeg_-722284921": "Identifier of a security assigned by the Japanese QUICK identification scheme for financial instruments.",
  "_Qdr_lNp-Ed-ak6NoX_4Aeg_1064399370": "Letters that identify a stock traded on a stock exchange. The Ticker Symbol is a short and convenient way of identifying a stock, eg, RTR.L for Reuters quoted in London.",
