  "_cH-V1znxEeabspMEjqY5TQ": "Identifier of securities issued in Luxembourg. The common code is a 9-digit code that replaces the CEDEL (Clearstream) and Euroclear codes.",
  "_cH-V2TnxEeabspMEjqY5TQ": "Proprietary identification of the security assigned by an institution or organisation.",
  "_cH1L4znxEeabspMEjqY5TQ": "International Securities Identification Number (ISIN). A numbering system designed by the United Nation's International Organisation for Standardisation (ISO). The ISIN is composed of a 2-character prefix representing the country of issue, followed by the national security number (if one exists), and a check digit. Each country has a national numbering agency that assigns ISIN numbers for securities in that country.",
  "_cH1L5TnxEeabspMEjqY5TQ": "Stock Exchange Daily Official List (SEDOL) number. A code used by the London Stock Exchange to identify foreign stocks, especially those that aren't actively traded in the US and don't have a CUSIP number.",
  "_cH1L5znxEeabspMEjqY5TQ": "Committee on Uniform Securities and Identification Procedures (CUSIP). The standards body that created and maintains the securities classification system in the US. The CUSIP is composed of a 9-character number that uniquely identifies a particular security. Non-US securities have a similar number called the CINS number.",
  "_cH1L6TnxEeabspMEjqY5TQ": "Reuters Identification Code (RIC). A numbering system used within the Reuters system to identify instruments worldwide. The RIC contains an X-character market specific code (can be the CUSIP or EPIC codes) followed by a full stop, then the two-digit ISO country code, for example, IBM in UK is IBM.UK.",
  "_cH1L6znxEeabspMEjqY5TQ": "Letters that identify a stock traded on a stock exchange. The Ticker Symbol is a short and convenient way of identifying a stock, for example, RTR.L for Reuters quoted in London.",
  "_cH1L7TnxEeabspMEjqY5TQ": "Identifier of a security assigned by the Bloomberg organisation.",
  "_cH1L7znxEeabspMEjqY5TQ": "Identifier of a security assigned by the Consolidated Tape Association.",
  "_cH1L8TnxEeabspMEjqY5TQ": "Identifier of a security assigned by the Japanese QUICK identification scheme for financial instruments.",
  "_cH1L8znxEeabspMEjqY5TQ": "Wertpapier Kenn-nummer. A number issued in Germany by the Wertpapier Mitteilungen. The Wertpapier Kenn-nummer, sometimes called WPK, contains 6-digits, but no check digit. There are different ranges of numbers representing different classes of securities.",
  "_cH1L9TnxEeabspMEjqY5TQ": "Identifier for Dutch securities.",
